          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The principle of functional extensionality states that two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equal"} equal
            if their values are equal at every argument.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#InSetTheory In set theory
          %p
            In set theory, in the same way that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            has internal and external versions, depending on whether one uses the
            %span.newWikiWord
              external logic
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/external+logic"} ?
            or the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
          %h4#external_function_extensionality External function extensionality
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝟙
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{1}
            denote
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniqueness+quantifier"} unique
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton"} singleton
            up to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
            = succeed "," do
              %strong external function extensionality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/element"} element
            in set theory:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                for all sets
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                and functions
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A \to B
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:A \to B
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo =
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = g
                if and only if for all elements
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in A
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) = g(x)
            %li
              %p
                for all sets
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                and functions
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A \to B
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:A \to B
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo =
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = g
                if and only if for all functions
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi 𝟙
                        %mo →
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:\mathbb{1} \to A
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi x
                        %mo =
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \circ x = g \circ x
            %li
              %p
                for all sets
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                and elements of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+set"} function set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi B
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in B^A
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi B
                          %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in B^A
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo =
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = g
                if and only if for all elements
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in A
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ev
                          %mrow
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ev
                          %mrow
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{ev}_{A, B}(f, x) = \mathrm{ev}_{A, B}(g, x)
            %li
              %p
                for all sets
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                and elements of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+set"} function set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi B
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in B^A
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi B
                          %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in B^A
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo =
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = g
                if and only if for all elements of the function set
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi A
                          %mi 𝟙
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in A^\mathbb{1}
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} comp
                          %mrow
                            %mi 𝟙
                            %mo ,
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} comp
                          %mrow
                            %mi 𝟙
                            %mo ,
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{comp}_{\mathbb{1}, A, B}(f, x) = \mathrm{comp}_{\mathbb{1}, A, B}(g, x)
          %p
            The first is the one most commonly found in foundations of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+set+theories"} categorical set theories
            with separate notions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/element"} element
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+set+theories"} categorical set theories
            where an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/element"} element
            is defined as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            out of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
            terminal set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝟙
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{1}
          %p
            The first and the third notions of function extensionality are equivalent to each other, since for every set theory with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+sets"} function sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sets"} category of sets
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
            between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Hom}(X, Y) \cong \mathrm{Hom}(1, Y^X)
          %p
            and thus for every function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:X \to Y
            there is a unique element of a function set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [f] \in Y^X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in Y^X
            there is a unique function
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ′
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g':X \to Y
          %h4#internal_function_extensionality Internal function extensionality
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝟙
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{1}
            denote
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniqueness+quantifier"} unique
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton"} singleton
            up to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
            and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{x \in A} B_x
            denote the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
            of a family of sets
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B_x)_{x \in A}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_{A}:A \to A \times A
            denote the
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal+function"} diagonal function
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preimage"} preimage
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_{A}
            at
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x, y) \in A \times A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi A
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_{A}^*(x, y)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsingleton"} subsingleton
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Delta_{A}^*(x, y))_{x \in A, y \in A}
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/family+of+sets"} family of sets
          %p
            The principle of
            %strong internal function extensionality
            is given by one of the two equivalent statements:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                given sets
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} funext
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo ,
                          %mi B
                      %mo ∈
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo ∈
                          %msup
                            %mi B
                            %mi A
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi g
                          %mo ∈
                          %msup
                            %mi B
                            %mi A
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi B
                            %mi A
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                            %mrow
                              %mi x
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi A
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi B
                            %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ev
                            %mrow
                              %mi A
                              %mo ,
                              %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo ,
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ev
                            %mrow
                              %mi A
                              %mo ,
                              %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi g
                          %mo ,
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{funext}_{A, B} \in \prod_{f \in B^A} \prod_{g \in B^A} \Delta_{B^A}^*(f, g)^{\prod_{x \in A} \Delta_{B}^*(\mathrm{ev}_{A, B}(f, x), \mathrm{ev}_{A, B}(g, x))}
            %li
              %p
                given sets
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} funext
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo ,
                          %mi B
                      %mo ∈
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo ∈
                          %msup
                            %mi B
                            %mi A
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi g
                          %mo ∈
                          %msup
                            %mi B
                            %mi A
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi B
                            %mi A
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                            %mrow
                              %mi x
                              %mo ∈
                              %msup
                                %mi A
                                %mi 𝟙
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi B
                                %mi 𝟙
                            %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} comp
                            %mrow
                              %mi 𝟙
                              %mo ,
                              %mi A
                              %mo ,
                              %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo ,
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} comp
                            %mrow
                              %mi 𝟙
                              %mo ,
                              %mi A
                              %mo ,
                              %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi g
                          %mo ,
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{funext}_{A, B} \in \prod_{f \in B^A} \prod_{g \in B^A} \Delta_{B^A}^*(f, g)^{\prod_{x \in A^\mathbb{1}} \Delta_{B^\mathbb{1}}^*(\mathrm{comp}_{\mathbb{1}, A, B}(f, x), \mathrm{comp}_{\mathbb{1}, A, B}(g, x))}
          %p
            This is the set theoretic analogue of the axiom of function extensionality found in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theories"} dependent type theories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal+subset"} diagonal
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-to-one+correspondence"} one-to-one correspondence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+products"} Cartesian products
            of arbitrary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/families+of+sets"} families of sets
            as well as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+sets"} function sets
          %h3#InCategoryTheory In category theory
          %h4#generalizing_external_function_extensionality Generalizing external function extensionality
          %p There are multiple ways to extend the set-theoretic definition of external function extensionality from the category of sets to more general categories.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The first notion of external function extensionality extends from the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sets"} category of sets
                to any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+category"} concrete category
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rings"} rings
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+homomorphisms"} group homomorphisms
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+homomorphisms"} ring homomorphisms
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+maps"} continuous maps
            %li
              %p
                The second notion of external function extensionality extends from the category of sets to any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-pointed+category"} well-pointed category
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
                is an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extremal+generator"} extremal generator
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopos"} pretopos
                a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-pointed+pretopos"} well-pointed pretopos
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+category"} concrete category
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
                is concrete but not well-pointed, while an arbitrary model of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ETCS"} ETCS
                is well-pointed but not necessarily concrete.
            %li
              %p
                The third and fourth notions of external function extensionality extends from the category of sets to any concrete
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed category
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p None of these notions are called “function extensionality” in category theory. The term “function extensionality” is reserved for the generalization of internal function extensionality to arbitrary categories, as documented in the next section.
          %h4#generalizing_internal_function_extensionality Generalizing internal function extensionality
          %p
            The notion of
            %strong function extensionality
            in a category arises from the generalization of the set-theoretic definition of internal function extensionality from the category of sets to more general categories. In particular, similar to internal function extensionality, it is the logical formulation of function extensionality in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+language"} internal language
            of the category. The “internal” formulation can be interpreted in a category with a rich enough
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+language"} internal language
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mitchell-Benabou+language"} Mitchell-Benabou language
            and is true in any
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            %em internally
            satisfies function extensionality despite the fact that toposes do not generally satisfy the external notion of being concrete or well-pointed. This is because the quantifier
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall x:X
            in the internal language is interpreted as a quantification over all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+elements"} generalized elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \to X
            rather than merely the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+elements"} global elements
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \to X
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+object"} exponential object
          %h3#InTypeTheory In dependent type theory
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intensional+type+theory"} intensional type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equality
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
