          %p where
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Maps
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Maps(X,Y)
                denotes the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
                in the ambient
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+model+of+dependent+types"} categorical model of dependent types
                —
              %p
                if one assumes a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closure
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+objects"} exponential objects
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Y
                          %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y^X
          %p
            So the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            of function extensionality
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:FunctionExtensionalityInTypeTheory"} (2)
            says in particular that there is a map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Paths
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi Maps
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Maps
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Paths
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\phi
                  \\;\colon\;
                  Paths\big(Maps(X,Y)\big)
                  \\longrightarrow
                  Maps\big(X, Paths(Y) \big)
          %p
            which serves to lift
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+elements"} global elements
            as above.
          %p
            Of course we are not just interested in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+element"} global elements
            here. What we really want is an actual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Maps
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Paths
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Paths
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi Maps
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Maps\big(X, Paths(Y)\big) \to Paths\big(Maps(X,Y)\big)
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Maps
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Maps\big(X, (Y \times Y)\big)
            (although this can be derived from the global element formulation by using the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
            together with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/currying"} currying
            and uncurrying tricks), such that this exhibits a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
          #FunExtInFibrationCat.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Function extensionality holds in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+language"} internal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type-theoretic+fibration+category"} type-theoretic fibration category
              precisely if
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+products"} dependent products
              (i.e. right
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
              preserve
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+fibrations"} acyclic fibrations
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Shulman12"}> Shulman 12, lemma 5.9
            )
          #EveryPresentableLocallyCartesinClosedInfinityCatInterpretsHoTTPlusFunExt.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              The condition in prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FunExtInFibrationCat"}
              holds in particular in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+proper+model+category"} right proper
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cisinski+model+structures"} Cisinski model structures
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
              along fibrations is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+Quillen+functor"} right Quillen functor
              (see e.g. the proof
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+(infinity,1)-category#PresentationTheorem"} here
            %p
              Notice that every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presentable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+Cartesian+closed+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} locally Cartesian closed (∞,1)-category
              (by the discussion
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "locally+cartesian+closed+(infinity,1)-category#PresentationTheorem"} there
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+proper+model+category"} right proper
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cisinski+model+category"} Cisinski model category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presentable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+Cartesian+closed+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} locally Cartesian closed (∞,1)-category
              interprets
              = succeed "+FunExt." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HoTT"} HoTT
          %h2#see_also See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensionality"} extensionality
            %li
