          %h2#References References
          %h3#ReferencesGeneral General
          %p
            Discussion of variants of function extensionality in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin-L%C3%B6f+type+theory"} Martin-Löf type theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Garner"}> Richard Garner
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the strength of dependent products in the type theory of Martin-Löf
                %strong 160
                1 (2009) 1-12 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0803.4466"}> arXiv:0803.4466
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apal.2008.12.003"} doi:10.1016/j.apal.2008.12.003
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+LeFanu+Lumsdaine"}> Peter LeFanu Lumsdaine
                ,
                %em Strong functional extensionality from weak
                (2011) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://homotopytypetheory.org/2011/12/19/strong-funext-from-weak"}> blog post
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#Rijke22"} Rijke (2022), §13.1
          %p
            Proofs of function extensionality from an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+type"} interval type
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgmental+equality"} judgmental
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computation+rules"} computation rules
          %ul
            %li#Shulman11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
              ,
              %em An interval type implies functional extensionality
              (2011) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://homotopytypetheory.org/2011/04/04/an-interval-type-implies-function-extensionality/"}> blog post
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#ReferencesInHomotopyTypeTheory In homotopy type theory
          %p
            Discussion of function extensionality in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            and proof that it is implied by
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence"} univalence
          %p Original announcement in:
          %ul
            %li#Voevodsky10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Voevodsky"}> Vladimir Voevodsky
              , p. 8 of:
              %em Univalent Foundations Project
              (2010) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.ias.edu/~vladimir/Site3/Univalent_Foundations_files/univalent_foundations_project.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Voevodsky-UFP2010.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li#UFP13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Univalent+Foundations+Project"}> Univalent Foundations Project
                , §2.9 &amp; §4.9
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopy+Type+Theory+--+Univalent+Foundations+of+Mathematics"} Homotopy Type Theory – Univalent Foundations of Mathematics
                (2013) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://homotopytypetheory.org/book/"}> web
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://hottheory.files.wordpress.com/2013/03/hott-online-323-g28e4374.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Rijke22
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Egbert+Rijke"}> Egbert Rijke
                , §13 in:
